  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Ionisation energy decreases with increase in the size of atom.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Rb</mi></math>&nbsp;belongs to alkali metal and down the group ionization energy decreases as size of atom increases down the group.&nbsp; Among the given elements,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sc</mi></math>&nbsp;being small has the highest ionization energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Na</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>496</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>419</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Sc</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>631</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
